Subject: drm/amdgpu: make the per-ASIC recovery defaults reachable again

amdgpu_device_should_recover_gpu() keeps a list of ASICs on which GPU
recovery is disabled when amdgpu.gpu_recovery is left at its default of
-1 (SI, CIK, Carrizo, Stoney, Cyan Skillfish). That list is not reached on
devices without a RAS context, because an earlier early return,

	/* Skip soft reset check in fatal error mode */
	if (!amdgpu_ras_is_poison_mode_supported(adev))
		return true;

returns true for every device whose RAS context is absent. The early return
was added by commit 1a11a65d5395 ("drm/amdgpu: Enable mode-1 reset for RAS
recovery in fatal error mode") to skip amdgpu_device_ip_check_soft_reset(),
which followed it at the time. Commit 360cd08196ca ("drm/amdgpu: adjust the
sequence to check soft reset") then moved that check out of this function,
so since then the early return skips nothing except the SR-IOV check, which
also returns true, and the per-ASIC list.

Observed on a Cyan Skillfish2 (1002:13fe, AMD BC-250) with kernel 7.1.8 and
amdgpu.gpu_recovery unset: a probe calling amdgpu_amdkfd_gpu_reset() reports
should_recover=1, the reset proceeds, and on this chip it takes the host down
(neither MODE1 nor MODE2 is implemented for it; see patch 2).

With the list reachable (tested as a reordering of the same checks), four
trials at the default that put a compute queue into a preemption failure
logged "GPU recovery disabled." for every KFD reset request, 69 per trial,
and the host stayed up.

Remove the stale early return so that devices without RAS reach the same
checks as everyone else. Devices not on the list are unaffected, since the
function returns true for them either way.

Fixes: 360cd08196ca ("drm/amdgpu: adjust the sequence to check soft reset")
---
Against torvalds/linux 587858367581 (2026-09-14). Evidence: logs/reset-smu-gc-2026-09-14/ and
logs/reset-path-2026-08-24/path-kfd_rep1.log, and the board test in
logs/reset-honest-2026-09-15/ (section C).

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
@@ -4901,10 +4901,6 @@
 	if (amdgpu_gpu_recovery == 0)
 		goto disabled;
 
-	/* Skip soft reset check in fatal error mode */
-	if (!amdgpu_ras_is_poison_mode_supported(adev))
-		return true;
-
 	if (amdgpu_sriov_vf(adev))
 		return true;
 
